---
title: "Withholding tax changes: check your November payslip"
date: 2026-11-03
lang: en
category: Payroll & HR
excerpt: "From 1 November, withholding tax calculation rules have changed: some employees gain a few euros, others lose out."
published: true
author: AgiFid
---

The Royal Decree of 27 September 2026 amends the calculation of withholding tax on income paid or allocated from 1 November 2026 onwards.
If you manage payroll for your employees, you must therefore verify that the new parameters have been correctly applied to the month's payslips.

## What's changing in practice

Three main modifications impact the calculation:

**1. The tax-exempt amount increases**

For withholding tax purposes, it rises from 11,170 euros to 11,550 euros for the 2026 income year.
This increase benefits all employees.

**2. The marital quotient is capped**

From November 2026, the calculation takes into account a marital quotient of 11,780 euros in principle, reached when the taxable net amount equals 39,266.67 euros.

The maximum amount thus attributed decreases from 13,790 to 11,780 euros per year.
This change penalises single-income couples.

**3. Child allowances change**

It increases from 624 to 684 euros per year for one child.
However,
it decreases from 1,656 to 1,644 euros for two children, from 4,404 to 4,344 euros for three and from 7,620 to 7,488 euros for four.

## The impact on net pay: who gains, who loses

Most employees will gain a few euros per month, but some will lose out.

**The gainers:**

Your withholding tax decreases by 8.47 euros per month, regardless of your gross salary. When both partners are employees, each receives this amount: the household therefore gains 16.94 euros per month.

A parent with two dependent children will receive approximately 1 euro less net each month, i.e. 7.47 euros extra in total.

**The losers:**

Single-income couples are most impacted by the reduction in the marital quotient.
Between 5,000 and 6,600 euros gross, your net pay decreases by 18.90 euros per month. Beyond approximately 6,800 euros gross, the loss reaches 27.86 euros per month.

Similarly, for large families (3 children or more), net salary decreases due to the temporary non-indexation and the freeze on supplements from the third child onwards.

## Who is concerned, who is not

These modifications apply only to employees' remuneration. In 2026, the withholding tax retained on pensions and on statutory unemployment benefits with company supplement has not yet been adapted and therefore remains unchanged.

The new rules apply to salaries paid or allocated from 1 November 2026 onwards, and previous months are not recalculated. However, an October salary paid in early November may already be affected.

## What you need to verify

If you use payroll software integrated with Odoo or a social secretariat, check that:

- Withholding tax parameters have been properly updated as at 1 November 2026
- November payslips reflect the new net amounts
- Your employees have properly declared their family situation (dependent children, marital status) to benefit from the correct allowances

The difference remains modest for most situations, but it directly impacts net pay received. A good time to remind your teams to check their payslips and report any changes in family circumstances.
